<p>This is a perfectly serviceable article, such that I feel comfortable novoting, but I have two concerns in particular.</p>
<p>Firstly, what are D-Class in your personal headcanon? The Ds in this article are so professional and amicable with Foundation personnel that they seem more like task force operatives. Having the Foundation not be essentially at war with their workforce is a valid headcanon, but this portrayal deviates so far from the norm that I feel it needs explicit clarification.</p>
<p>Secondly, the redactions. The Foundation covering something up for ethical reasons is also valid, although it does seem to contradict the whole &quot;amicable D-Class&quot; idea you have elsewhere. But I don't think they'd cover up the truth about an anomaly; ethical redactions would be saved for when the Foundation itself has done something terrible. Maybe that borders on personal headcanon, but when you deal in existential threats, I doubt the revelation that the dust is people would be particularly disconcerting, and not something they'd want to specifically redact. If anything, I think the Foundation knowing that we are the dust and not really caring is a greater expression of horror and worldbuilding than what's right here.</p>

