														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4494807">
									

<p>I really like this! I'll try to point out what makes it work for me:</p>
<ul>
<li>The logs are well written and it becomes clear very quickly that their confusing nature is purposeful (as well as not so exaggerated that they become incomprehensible). They also characterize everyone well enough that I'd love to read other stories with Mai or even 26 and 99.</li>
<li>The big mystery of what exactly the anomaly does was hinted at enough that I managed to get it at just the right time, near the end of the article, during 99's final speech. I'm not exactly the best at solving these types of mysteries, usually having to rely on either the author or some other user to explain or theorize about the explanation, but this time it was clear enough even for me.</li>
<li>The note at the end and the punishment given to Dr. Mai felt like more of a cruelty than detached coldness from Ashby, and from reading the comments here, that seems to have been your intention so I think you succeeded there too (also, 99 saying &quot;you're going to be crushed, Dr. Mai&quot; felt almost like some foreshadowing of this). That being said, I'm a fan of a more human characterization of the Foundation, whether the human aspect in question is positive or negative, so I like seeing this dynamic of a &quot;rookie&quot; Foundation doctor who still sees the D-class as human vs. an older much more cruel Dr. who sees them as mere objects to use in testing. Others who prefer the more cold and distant Foundation might not enjoy this as much.</li>
</ul>
<p>+1 and hope to see more of Dr. Mai in the future, the character has good potential.</p>

							</div>

								
					
